              ].filter(Boolean).join(', ')}. Treasury certification remains the authoritative record.
              {nomination.list_published_url && (
                <a href={nomination.list_published_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-oz-blue underline"> See the published list →</a>
              )}
              {nomination.source_url && !nomination.list_published_url && (
                <a href={nomination.source_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-oz-blue underline"> Source →</a>
              )}
            </p>
          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="mb-4 border-l-4 border-oz-neutral-300 bg-oz-neutral-50 pl-4 py-3 pr-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-oz-neutral-700">
              {name} has not published the tract list it submitted, as of {nomination.last_checked}.
              That is the norm — most states are waiting for Treasury to certify before releasing a
              slate. The lead agency below is the place to ask.
            </p>
          </div>
        )}
        <p class="text-sm text-oz-neutral-700 mb-3">
          Designations take effect {fmt(DATES.designationsEffective)} and run through {fmt(DATES.designationsExpire)}.
          {name} could nominate up to {max_designations.toLocaleString()} of its {total_eligible.toLocaleString()} eligible
          tracts, so most eligible tracts here will not be designated.
